**Convention 4.1 (entry correspondence obligations).** The relevant
installed-entry clauses have the following parameter map.

| Actual source clause | Supplied fact | Obligation at the added cuts used here |
| --- | --- | --- |
| AIF Definition 2.6 | Original prescribed IN/non-IN experiments and finite lawful semantic protocols, with the original partial response meanings. | Identify an added row as that prescribed original action; raw native enabledness alone is insufficient. |
| CAP Definition 4.6 | Resident source admission at acknowledged idle; journal entry through its actually installed public caller or the producer's held frozen-prefix continuation. No arbitrary-busy-cut journal entry is granted. | Establish the actual caller/PC/phase/token relation for any proposed original source or audit invocation during annex work. A source token at its dispatcher does not identify that entry. |
| ARC Definitions 4.1 and 5.1–5.3 | Parked original client, outer Ready relation, gate dispatch, invocation transfer and native70 history ingress. | Relate the resulting handler-owned history phase to an original experiment, rather than merely to its own native next row. |
| GCA Definitions 2.2 and 3.1 | Actual latch4 public reads, latch6 ingress, mode seal/import and subsequent frame import. | Establish the original Advance judgment at EX70 and along the finite completion/LastBank segment, preserving actual original successor fields. |
| SOURCECALL Lemma 2.3 and GENERAL Theorem 9.1 | Direct original correspondence inside unchanged $F^A$, at a fixed actual reached entry, excluding the changed final idle CTL. | These hypotheses do not hold at the history-ingress cuts of Definition 2.1 or the mode cut of §6. |
| ARC Definition 11.1, UAS Definition 1.4 and GENERAL obligation 10.3 | $Q$ uses the original installed relation; $Q_G$ additionally exposes new history entries. Added-phase original correspondence is a separate obligation. | Supply the selected original admission/domain/response cases; neither universal admission nor universal unexecuted `none` follows from the distinction. |

In particular, the next raw row after $x_i$ is EX70, and the handler holds
the history invocation while the original client is parked. The original
source frame has not thereby been admitted. AIF's permission to finish
an already admitted original request cannot be applied just by renaming
this history request. Conversely, these facts do not prove that every
original semantic/audit experiment is unavailable. Its actual entry
must be checked on its own source clauses.

